{"book":9,"chapter":23,"rubric":"DATABASES / SCALE AND CONSISTENCY / CHAPTER 23","slides":[{"title":"Why split","sub":"Chapter 23 · Sharding","short":"Introduction","main":"Replication copies; sharding splits data across machines.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["One server","Splitting","Replication ≠ sharding"],"captions":["Data does not fit on one machine, or writes hit the leader's disk limit: replication will not help","Sharding: each machine stores only part of the data, its own shard (partition)","Replication copies the same data; sharding splits different data; in practice they are combined"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":180.0,"y":76.0,"w":140.0,"h":50.0,"text":"server\ndisk 100%","tone":"red","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":76.0,"w":70.0,"h":30.0,"text":"shard 1\n0–33%","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":76.0,"w":70.0,"h":30.0,"text":"shard 2\n33–66%","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":290.0,"y":76.0,"w":70.0,"h":30.0,"text":"shard 3\n66–100%","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":50.0,"w":66.0,"h":30.0,"text":"shard 1","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":90.0,"y":100.0,"w":66.0,"h":30.0,"text":"copy 1","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":50.0,"w":66.0,"h":30.0,"text":"shard 2","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b2","x":270.0,"y":100.0,"w":66.0,"h":30.0,"text":"copy 2","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":90.0,"y1":66.0,"x2":90.0,"y2":86.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":270.0,"y1":66.0,"x2":270.0,"y2":86.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[16.6,34.3]}]},{"title":"Shard key","sub":"The main decision","short":"Key","main":"The key must appear in queries and spread the load evenly.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Key","Must be in qu